    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "A family were stuck in their house after a serious storm. During the storm, the clock was damaged so that only the hour hand worked. The family stayed inside the house for 636 hours after the storm. How many times did the hour hand go around the clock before they left?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "53 times",
      "worked": "The hour hand completes one revolution every 12 hours.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}636\\div12&=(600+36)\\div12\\\\636\\div12&=50+3\\\\636\\div12&=53\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe hour hand went around the clock 53 times.",
